{"record_id":"D21-B21-001","batch_id":"D21-B21","domain":"performance","topic":"CPU hotspot isolation","knowledge_type":"profiling_method","language":"Python","concept":"A performance optimization should begin by identifying the dominant CPU-consuming call path rather than optimizing code based on intuition.","implementation_pattern":"Profile representative workloads and rank cumulative execution time and call frequency before modifying implementation.","code_example":"def transform(items):\n    return [normalize(parse(x)) for x in items]\n\n# Profile the representative workload with cProfile rather than timing one invocation.","expected_behavior":"The optimization target should be selected from measured workload data and should correspond to a meaningful fraction of total execution time.","anti_pattern":"Optimizing a rarely executed helper because its local implementation looks inefficient.","performance_effect":"Prevents optimization effort from being spent on non-dominant code paths.","verification_method":"Compare profiler output before and after the change using the same workload and environment.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"DOCUMENTED","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"Python >=3.11","provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python Debugging and Profiling documentation","source_version":"3.14.7"}}
{"record_id":"D21-B21-002","batch_id":"D21-B21","domain":"performance","topic":"microbenchmark isolation","knowledge_type":"benchmarking_method","language":"Python","concept":"Small code fragments should be measured with a controlled microbenchmark when the question concerns operation-level timing.","implementation_pattern":"Use repeated measurements with an isolated benchmark instead of measuring a single wall-clock invocation.","code_example":"from timeit import timeit\n\nseconds = timeit(\"sum(range(1000))\", number=10000)","expected_behavior":"Repeated execution reduces the influence of one-off timing noise and makes alternatives easier to compare.","anti_pattern":"Using one datetime difference to conclude that a micro-optimization is faster.","performance_effect":"Improves measurement reliability for small operations.","verification_method":"Run equivalent benchmark cases under the same interpreter, workload, and environment; inspect distributions rather than relying on one sample.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"DOCUMENTED","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"Python >=3.11","provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python Debugging and Profiling documentation","source_version":"3.14.7"}}
