{"record_id":"D21-B22-001","batch_id":"D21-B22","domain":"performance","topic":"allocation pressure","knowledge_type":"optimization_pattern","language":"Python","concept":"Repeated temporary object creation can increase CPU and memory-management overhead in allocation-heavy paths.","implementation_pattern":"Reduce unnecessary intermediate objects while preserving clarity and semantics.","code_example":"# Avoid constructing multiple intermediate collections when one traversal is sufficient.\nresult = [f(x) for x in items if predicate(x)]","expected_behavior":"The implementation performs the required transformation without retaining unnecessary intermediate collections.","anti_pattern":"Creating several full-size temporary lists solely to feed the next transformation.","performance_effect":"Can reduce peak memory usage and allocation overhead for large workloads.","verification_method":"Compare peak memory and runtime on representative large inputs.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLE","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"Python >=3.11"}
{"record_id":"D21-B22-002","batch_id":"D21-B22","domain":"performance","topic":"streaming versus materialization","knowledge_type":"optimization_pattern","language":"Python","concept":"When consumers do not require the entire result simultaneously, lazy iteration can avoid materializing a complete collection.","implementation_pattern":"Use an iterator or generator when downstream processing can consume items incrementally.","code_example":"def records(source):\n    for item in source:\n        yield normalize(item)","expected_behavior":"Only the items consumed by downstream logic are generated and retained.","anti_pattern":"Building a complete list of millions of records when downstream logic processes them one at a time.","performance_effect":"Can substantially reduce peak memory consumption and enable incremental processing.","verification_method":"Measure peak resident memory and verify identical logical outputs.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLE","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"Python >=3.11"}
{"record_id":"D21-B22-003","batch_id":"D21-B22","domain":"performance","topic":"memory locality","knowledge_type":"optimization_concept","language":"C++","concept":"Data layouts that improve locality can reduce cache-miss overhead in hot loops.","implementation_pattern":"Prefer data-oriented layouts when the workload repeatedly processes the same fields across many objects.","code_example":"struct Particles {\n    std::vector<float> x;\n    std::vector<float> y;\n    std::vector<float> z;\n};","expected_behavior":"A loop processing one coordinate field can access contiguous values rather than traversing unrelated object fields.","anti_pattern":"Using a pointer-rich object graph in a cache-sensitive numeric traversal without evidence that the layout is appropriate.","performance_effect":"May improve cache locality and reduce memory-access overhead.","verification_method":"Profile cache-sensitive workloads and compare equivalent layouts under identical conditions.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLE","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"C++17+"}
