{"record_id":"D21-B50-002","batch_id":"D21-B50","domain":"performance","topic":"performance contradiction handling","knowledge_type":"reasoning_pattern","language":"multi-language","concept":"Two optimization records can both be correct under different workloads, runtimes, data sizes, or resource constraints.","implementation_pattern":"Preserve contradictory observations with their workload and environment context instead of deduplicating them into one universal rule.","example":"Batching may improve throughput for large independent operations while increasing latency for interactive single-item requests.","expected_behavior":"The knowledge system retrieves the applicable record based on workload context.","anti_pattern":"Deleting one observation because it conflicts with another without checking their experimental conditions.","performance_effect":"Prevents context-specific performance knowledge from becoming misleading generalized rules.","verification_method":"Compare workload, runtime, hardware, dependency, and metric definitions before resolving apparent contradictions.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"REVIEWED","evidence_level":"ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLE","confidence":"HIGH","version_range":"Language-independent"}

